# Vendored font assets (app/_fonts). See FONTS.md.

# The .woff2 files are the exact bytes the previous next/font/google build
# served. Mark them binary explicitly so no future core.autocrlf or diff
# setting can rewrite a byte and silently corrupt a face.
*.woff2 binary

# The OFL 1.1 notices must stay byte-for-byte as their upstream projects
# publish them - undercasetype/Fraunces ships a line with a trailing space.
# `git diff --check` (which this repo runs in verify:prepush) would flag it,
# and "fixing" it would mean editing a licence text to satisfy a linter.
# Exempt them from the whitespace check instead, and keep them verbatim.
#
# They live in public/ because they must reach the BROWSER, not just the
# checkout: OFL 1.1 clause 2 requires the licence to accompany each distributed
# copy of the Font Software, and the served .woff2 subsets carry only the
# copyright (name ID 0) and a licence URL (name ID 14) - Google's subsetting
# strips the licence body (name ID 13). Next serves public/ verbatim, so these
# are reachable at /fonts/LICENSE-*.txt in the deployed app. See FONTS.md.
public/fonts/LICENSE-*.txt -whitespace
